in late March a Navajo tribal member  learned she had been exposed to  coronavirus and sucked testing at an  Indian Health Service or IHS hospital  they were me away and told me that I  didn't have any symptoms that night  around midnight I started to run fevers  and the next day the body aches started  they were so excruciating like every  bone in my body was hurting all the way  down to the tip of my toes to the tip of  my fingers with very very bad headaches  Farah Begay returned to the IHS hospital  but they refused to admit her or her 66  year old mother who was also ill they  turned us away and told us that come  back until it gets worse and you know at  that point you're like what is worse me  what's worse than this it's gonna get  worse than this the IHS is run by the  federal government in Washington it is  notoriously underfunded understaffed and  under equipped we asked the IHS  repeatedly over several weeks for an  interview but got nowhere we don't have  the best health care system on a Navajo  Nation we have been hit hard by this  virus that has snuck into our  communities here on the Navajo Nation  Navajo lands are impoverished rural and  arid basic infrastructure is shockingly  bad you know you got the CDC saying wash  your hands with soap and water everybody  but you know what 30% of our Navajo  people do not have running water  he says Native American communities  aren't getting the emergency money they  need for testing and equipment we're  just kidding just little bits of funding  to our nation's and that's all the all  the tribes throughout the country it  just seems like the first citizens of  this country have been ignored  once again on  fourth visit to the IHS barely able to  breathe Begay pleaded desperately for  help we're already feeling pain and fear  so when is worse gonna be worse until  we're dead she and her mother were  finally taken to better equipped  hospitals in Arizona after weeks they  have now recovered but many Navajo have  not I've known people personally from  this community that were turned away  like that went home and died in their  own homes the first Americans once again  last in line for help  Rob Reynolds al-jazeera
 

